CLASS:: Neutron
summary:: MIDI configuration for Behringer Neutron synthesizer
categories:: External Control>MIDI
related:: Classes/MIDIOut

DESCRIPTION::
Neutron provides a convenient interface for configuring the Behringer Neutron synthesizer via MIDI. It handles common configuration tasks like setting split keyboard mode, note priority, and sending notes with pitch bend.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Create a new Neutron instance with an existing MIDIOut object.

ARGUMENT:: midiOut
A MIDIOut object connected to the Neutron.

ARGUMENT:: channel
MIDI channel (0-15). Default is 0.

returns:: A new Neutron instance.

METHOD:: connect
Automatically find and connect to a Neutron MIDI device.

ARGUMENT:: channel
MIDI channel (0-15). Default is 0.

returns:: A new Neutron instance, or nil if Neutron not found.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: setSplitMode
Configure keyboard split mode.

ARGUMENT:: splitNote
MIDI note number (0-127) where the split occurs. Notes below this go to one voice, notes at or above go to another. Default is 60 (middle C).

ARGUMENT:: enable
Boolean to enable (true) or disable (false) split mode. Default is true.

returns:: this (for method chaining)

METHOD:: setNotePriority
Set the note priority mode for monophonic playing.

ARGUMENT:: priority
Symbol: code::\lowest::, code::\highest::, or code::\last::. Default is code::\lowest::.

returns:: this (for method chaining)

METHOD:: allNotesOff
Send all notes off and reset all controllers.

returns:: this (for method chaining)

METHOD:: resetBend
Reset pitch bend to center position (8192).

returns:: this (for method chaining)

METHOD:: noteOn
Send a note on message with pitch bend.

ARGUMENT:: note
MIDI note number (0-127).

ARGUMENT:: bend
Pitch bend value (0-16383, center is 8192). Default is 8192.

ARGUMENT:: velocity
Note velocity (0-127). Default is 127.

returns:: this (for method chaining)

METHOD:: noteOff
Send a note off message.

ARGUMENT:: note
MIDI note number (0-127).

ARGUMENT:: velocity
Release velocity (0-127). Default is 0.

returns:: this (for method chaining)

METHOD:: printInfo
Print current MIDI configuration to the post window.

returns:: this

EXAMPLES::

code::
// Automatically connect to Neutron
~neutron = Neutron.connect(channel: 0);

// Configure split keyboard at middle C with lowest note priority
~neutron.setSplitMode(60, true).setNotePriority(\lowest);

// Play a note with pitch bend
~neutron.noteOn(60, 8351, 127);

// Turn off all notes
~neutron.allNotesOff;

// Manual connection with existing MIDIOut
MIDIClient.init;
~midiOut = MIDIOut(0);
~neutron = Neutron(~midiOut, channel: 0);
~neutron.setNotePriority(\highest);
::
